{"id": "unknown-2026-09-09-015", "date": "2026-09-09", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q3", "month": 9, "week": 37, "weekday": "Wed"}, "entities": {"companies": [], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["industry_general"], "sentiment": {"label": "positive", "score": 1.0, "keywords": ["dominant"]}, "importance": {"score": 0.65, "reasons": ["情緒極端"]}, "title": "Africa’s solar panel manufacturing capacity to reach 3.5 GW this year", "content": "<p>Report from Ember and Africa Tech Futures Lab says solar panel manufacturing output will reach around 3.5 GW in 2026, led by new plants in Egypt and Tanzania that are geared predominantly towards US export.</p>\n<p>The post <a href=\"https://www.pv-magazine.com/2026/09/09/africas-solar-panel-manufacturing-capacity-to-reach-3-5-gw-this-year/\">Africa’s solar panel manufacturing capacity to reach 3.5 GW this year</a> appeared first on <a href=\"https://www.pv-magazine.com\">pv magazine Global</a>.</", "sources": [{"name": "pv_magazine", "url": "https://www.pv-magazine.com/2026/09/09/africas-solar-panel-manufacturing-capacity-to-reach-3-5-gw-this-year/", "type": "rss"}]}
{"id": "sungrow-2026-09-09-016", "date": "2026-09-09", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q3", "month": 9, "week": 37, "weekday": "Wed"}, "entities": {"companies": ["sungrow"], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["industry_general"], "sentiment": {"label": "positive", "score": 0.5, "keywords": ["expand"]}, "importance": {"score": 0.5, "reasons": []}, "title": "Sungrow turns to Samsung SDI battery cells to sustain its energy storage business", "content": "<p>ungrow plans to procure Samsung SDI battery cells for its energy storage systems, primarily to support continued deliveries to the U.S. market amid tightening restrictions on China-linked supply chains.<br />\nThe potential three-year, multi-GWh LFP deal could leverage Samsung SDI’s expanding U.S. production footprint, although procurement volumes, manufacturing locations and commercial terms remain undisclosed.</p>\n<p>The post <a href=\"https://www.pv-magazine.com/2026/09/09/sungrow-turns-to-s", "sources": [{"name": "pv_magazine", "url": "https://www.pv-magazine.com/2026/09/09/sungrow-turns-to-samsung-sdi-battery-cells-to-sustain-its-energy-storage-business/", "type": "rss"}]}
{"id": "unknown-2026-09-09-017", "date": "2026-09-09", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q3", "month": 9, "week": 37, "weekday": "Wed"}, "entities": {"companies": [], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["industry_general"], "sentiment": {"label": "neutral", "score": 0.0, "keywords": []}, "importance": {"score": 0.5, "reasons": []}, "title": "Switzerland’s largest battery storage facility goes online", "content": "<p>Switzerland’s largest battery storage facility has begun operations in Gurtnellen, combining 50 MW and 8.4 MW systems developed by Axpo and Energie Uri. The Fluence-supplied project will support grid flexibility.</p>\n<p>The post <a href=\"https://www.pv-magazine.com/2026/09/09/switzerlands-largest-battery-storage-facility-goes-online/\">Switzerland&#8217;s largest battery storage facility goes online</a> appeared first on <a href=\"https://www.pv-magazine.com\">pv magazine Global</a>.</p>\n", "sources": [{"name": "pv_magazine", "url": "https://www.pv-magazine.com/2026/09/09/switzerlands-largest-battery-storage-facility-goes-online/", "type": "rss"}]}
{"id": "unknown-2026-09-09-018", "date": "2026-09-09", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q3", "month": 9, "week": 37, "weekday": "Wed"}, "entities": {"companies": [], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["industry_general"], "sentiment": {"label": "neutral", "score": 0.0, "keywords": []}, "importance": {"score": 0.5, "reasons": []}, "title": "From more than 50 GW to under 10 GW: Ukraine doesn’t need its old energy system back", "content": "<p>Six air-raid alerts on the first day, backup generators on almost every street corner, and discussions about the rapid reconstruction of severely damaged energy infrastructure: my trip to Kyiv and Lviv showed me why decentralized solar and energy storage are far more than climate technologies for Ukraine. They are part of the country’s security architecture. They also underscore why German solar companies should be engaging with Ukraine today.</p>\n<p>The post <a href=\"https://www.pv-magazine.", "sources": [{"name": "pv_magazine", "url": "https://www.pv-magazine.com/2026/09/09/from-more-than-50-to-just-under-10-gigawatts-ukraine-does-not-need-its-old-energy-system-back/", "type": "rss"}]}
{"id": "unknown-2026-09-09-019", "date": "2026-09-09", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q3", "month": 9, "week": 37, "weekday": "Wed"}, "entities": {"companies": [], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["industry_general"], "sentiment": {"label": "positive", "score": 0.5, "keywords": ["increase"]}, "importance": {"score": 0.5, "reasons": []}, "title": "EU policymakers look to raise IAA Made in Europe threshold to 50%", "content": "<p>The EU's rapporteurs on the proposed Industrial Accelerator Act are also calling for increased EU content in solar panels and for stricter component requirements against circumvention.</p>\n<p>The post <a href=\"https://www.pv-magazine.com/2026/09/09/eu-policymakers-look-to-raise-iaa-made-in-europe-threshold-to-50/\">EU policymakers look to raise IAA Made in Europe threshold to 50%</a> appeared first on <a href=\"https://www.pv-magazine.com\">pv magazine Global</a>.</p>\n", "sources": [{"name": "pv_magazine", "url": "https://www.pv-magazine.com/2026/09/09/eu-policymakers-look-to-raise-iaa-made-in-europe-threshold-to-50/", "type": "rss"}]}
{"id": "unknown-2026-09-09-020", "date": "2026-09-09", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q3", "month": 9, "week": 37, "weekday": "Wed"}, "entities": {"companies": [], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["installation_demand", "industry_general"], "sentiment": {"label": "neutral", "score": 0.0, "keywords": []}, "importance": {"score": 0.5, "reasons": []}, "title": "France’s installed PV capacity hits 34 GW", "content": "<p>France connected 3 GW of new solar capacity in the first half of 2026, slightly above the 2.9 GW deployed in the same period of 2025. Large-scale installations above 500 kW accounted for 28% of newly connected capacity, despite representing just 0.3% of new connections. Systems below 9 kW dominated installation numbers, accounting for 78% of new connections but only 8% of added capacity. </p>\n<p>The post <a href=\"https://www.pv-magazine.com/2026/09/09/frances-pv-capacity-reaches-34-gw/\">Franc", "sources": [{"name": "pv_magazine", "url": "https://www.pv-magazine.com/2026/09/09/frances-pv-capacity-reaches-34-gw/", "type": "rss"}]}
{"id": "unknown-2026-09-09-021", "date": "2026-09-09", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q3", "month": 9, "week": 37, "weekday": "Wed"}, "entities": {"companies": [], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["industry_general"], "sentiment": {"label": "neutral", "score": 0.0, "keywords": ["growth", "weak"]}, "importance": {"score": 0.5, "reasons": []}, "title": "Italian solar redrew the day, but gas still sets the price", "content": "<p>Solar growth softened Italy’s midday power squeeze in summer 2026, but higher heat-driven demand and weaker hydro and wind left gas to cover most of the 7.9 TWh supply gap. The result was a sharper evening exposure: gas generation surged, prices rose most after sunset, and solar-heavy southern zones increasingly faced midday oversupply and weaker capture rates.</p>\n<p>The post <a href=\"https://www.pv-magazine.com/2026/09/09/italian-solar-redrew-the-day-but-gas-still-sets-the-price/\">Italian s", "sources": [{"name": "pv_magazine", "url": "https://www.pv-magazine.com/2026/09/09/italian-solar-redrew-the-day-but-gas-still-sets-the-price/", "type": "rss"}]}
{"id": "unknown-2026-09-09-022", "date": "2026-09-09", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q3", "month": 9, "week": 37, "weekday": "Wed"}, "entities": {"companies": [], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["industry_general"], "sentiment": {"label": "neutral", "score": 0.0, "keywords": []}, "importance": {"score": 0.5, "reasons": []}, "title": "Sodium-ion storage powers fully off-grid solar home in Germany", "content": "<p>A homeowner in Augsburg has paired 270 kWh of BIWATT sodium-ion storage with 49 kWp of solar, creating a fully off-grid household energy system with local distributor SALZSTROM providing the solution.</p>\n<p>The post <a href=\"https://www.pv-magazine.com/2026/09/09/sodium-ion-storage-powers-fully-off-grid-solar-home-in-germany/\">Sodium-ion storage powers fully off-grid solar home in Germany</a> appeared first on <a href=\"https://www.pv-magazine.com\">pv magazine Global</a>.</p>\n", "sources": [{"name": "pv_magazine", "url": "https://www.pv-magazine.com/2026/09/09/sodium-ion-storage-powers-fully-off-grid-solar-home-in-germany/", "type": "rss"}]}
{"id": "unknown-2026-09-09-023", "date": "2026-09-09", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q3", "month": 9, "week": 37, "weekday": "Wed"}, "entities": {"companies": [], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["industry_general"], "sentiment": {"label": "neutral", "score": 0.0, "keywords": []}, "importance": {"score": 0.5, "reasons": []}, "title": "Reliability risks emerge across BIPV, floating PV and agrivoltaics", "content": "<p>A new IEA PVPS Task 13 report identifies distinct reliability risks across BIPV, floating PV and agrivoltaics, from heat and partial shading to wave loads, ammonia exposure and soiling. It argues that existing PV qualification standards do not fully capture these application-specific stresses, requiring adapted testing, design practices and performance metrics.</p>\n<p>The post <a href=\"https://www.pv-magazine.com/2026/09/09/reliability-risks-emerge-across-bipv-floating-pv-and-agrivoltaics/\">R", "sources": [{"name": "pv_magazine", "url": "https://www.pv-magazine.com/2026/09/09/reliability-risks-emerge-across-bipv-floating-pv-and-agrivoltaics/", "type": "rss"}]}
{"id": "unknown-2026-09-09-024", "date": "2026-09-09", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q3", "month": 9, "week": 37, "weekday": "Wed"}, "entities": {"companies": [], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["installation_demand", "industry_general"], "sentiment": {"label": "neutral", "score": 0.0, "keywords": []}, "importance": {"score": 0.5, "reasons": []}, "title": "Netherlands installs 1.4 GW of solar in 2025", "content": "<p>Official statistics from the Netherlands show the drop in annual solar installations last year was larger than estimates indicated. Annual deployments are now forecast to stabilise around 1.3 GW through to 2028.</p>\n<p>The post <a href=\"https://www.pv-magazine.com/2026/09/09/the-netherlands-installs-1-4-gw-of-solar-in-2025/\">Netherlands installs 1.4 GW of solar in 2025</a> appeared first on <a href=\"https://www.pv-magazine.com\">pv magazine Global</a>.</p>\n", "sources": [{"name": "pv_magazine", "url": "https://www.pv-magazine.com/2026/09/09/the-netherlands-installs-1-4-gw-of-solar-in-2025/", "type": "rss"}]}
